{{Quote|<nowiki></nowiki>''Bane Malar.'' A bounty hunter who, when given the option to deliver his quarry 'dead or alive,' invariably chose the ''former''. By returning with only their ''heads''.|Eightyem|<ref name="Jabba's Palace 1" />}}
'''Bane Malar''' was a [[Gender|male]] [[bounty hunter]] who specialized in tracking those who escaped the [[Spice mines of Kessel|Spice Mines]] of [[Kessel]]. A natural [[Telepathy|telepath]], Malar would use [[glitterstim]] to enhance his abilities, which allowed him to invade the minds of those he was hunting down.<ref name="FC" /> In [[4 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{SW|url=news/the-illustrious-jabba-the-hutt-bids-you-welcome-to-his-new-marvel-comic-jabbas-palace-exclusive-reveal|text=The Illustrious Jabba the Hutt Bids You Welcome to His New Marvel Comic, ''Jabba's Palace'' - Exclusive Reveal}} establishes that [[Star Wars: Return of the Jedi (2023)|''Star Wars: Return of the Jedi'']] takes place in the era of {{Film|VI}}, which ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates to [[4 ABY]].</ref> Malar was present in [[Boba Fett's Palace|Jabba's Palace]] during [[80-M|Eightyem's]] [[time]] as [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]]'s [[translator droid]].<ref name="Jabba's Palace 1" />

==Biography==
===The Silvan Kaan affair===
{{Quote|As it is, Mr. Malar, I'm unclear as to what you want me to tell you.''"<br />"''You think you've been ''subtle''? You think I haven't seen you having whispered conversations in quiet corners with that Twi'lek?''"<br />"''My purview as Jabba's translator often requires me to converse with Mr. Fortuna&mdash;''"<br />"''Not Fortuna. ''Silvan Kaan''. The guy's so slippery, those head-tails of his might as well be ''serpents''.|Eightyem and Bane Malar|<ref name="Jabba's Palace 1" />}}
The [[Gender|male]]<ref name="FC" /> Bane Malar was present in the [[Boba Fett's Palace|palace]] of [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba the Hutt]] when the [[crime lord]] was visited by [[Twi'lek]] [[criminal]] [[Silvan Kaan]]<ref name="Jabba's Palace 1" /> in [[4 ABY]].<ref name="Date" /> Malar grew suspicious of Kaan and Jabba's [[translator droid]], [[80-M|Eightyem]], whom Kaan had persuaded into a partnership. The [[bounty hunter]] took Eightyem aside and, instructing the [[droid]] not to lie, confronted him about his actions. Though Malar made direct accusations towards the droid, the interpreter maintained a façade of ignorance, causing the bounty hunter to admit his own uncertainty as to the violations committed. Malar then told Eightyem that he would discover the truth of the matter. Eightyem informed Kaan of what had transpired, though the Twi'lek remained unconcerned.<ref name="Jabba's Palace 1" />

Malar later foiled an attempt on Jabba's life by [[Charn Roondha]], an [[Ithorian]] who collected taxes imposed by the [[Hutt]]. The bounty hunter held the would-be [[assassin]] at the point of his own weapon, a [[WESTAR-35 blaster pistol]] that Malar noted Roondha was likely not cleared to have on his person, a fact confirmed by Jabba's aide, [[Bib Fortuna]]. The weapon had indeed been smuggled in by Eightyem on Kaan's suggestion.<ref name="Jabba's Palace 1" />

===Apprehending Kaan===
{{Quote|I hear the ''Great Pit of Carkoon's'' just ''lovely'' this time of year.''"<br />"''Mr. Malar, whatever it is you ''think'' you've seen&mdash;''"<br />"''Oh, no thinking involved. ''[Malar produces a hologram]'' &hellip;We're talking here about ''knowing''.|Bane Malar and Silvan Kaan|<ref name="Jabba's Palace 1" />}}
Malar accompanied Jabba's posse aboard the Hutt's [[sail barge]], the ''[[Khetanna]]'', to the [[Great Pit of Carkoon]] out in the [[Dune Sea]], where Roondha was fed to [[Almighty Sarlacc|the]] [[sarlacc]] that nested there. The bounty hunter commented on the Ithorian's demise and made a veiled threat toward Kaan about joining the tax collector in the sarlacc's gut, where he would be digested over the course of a thousand years. Malar then told Kaan to enjoy the party and departed.<ref name="Jabba's Palace 1" />

Sometime later at Jabba's Palace, Malar ambushed Kaan as he removed Eightyem's restraining bolt, training his sniper rifle on the Twi'lek. The bounty hunter suggested that the criminal take a trip back to the Great Pit of Carkoon, presenting him with a holographic recording of Eightyem's transgressions. Kaan was brought before Jabba, who indeed condemned the man to the sarlacc for his deceptions, while Eightyem was sentenced to disintegration on [[supervisor droid]] [[EV-9D9]]'s torture rack for his own treachery.<ref name="Jabba's Palace 1" />

===Hunting a reprobate===
{{Quote|If you kill me, Jabba's never getting the 50,000 credits&mdash;''"<br />"''80,000.''"<br />"''80,000 credits I owe him.''"<br />"''Jabba knows you'll never be able to pay that back in a ''lifetime''. Which is why he wants ''yours'' cut short&mdash;|Bane Malar and Rik Duel|<ref name="Duel">{{StoryCite|story=Duel of the Reprobates|book=Revelations (2023) 1}}</ref>}}
Malar tracked down the scoundrel [[Rik Duel]] on Jabba's behalf. Duel convinced Malar that he was worth more alive than dead, resulting in Duel becoming Jabba's "top lieutenant."<ref name="Duel" />

==Skills and abilities==
{{Quote|Is there a problem, Mr. Malar?''"<br />"''You tell me, droid. And don't ''lie''. I'm too smart for you to outsmart&mdash;so you best not ''try''.|Bane Malar to Eightyem|<ref name="Jabba's Palace 1" />}}
Bane Malar maintained a career as a bounty hunter<ref name="Jabba's Palace 1" /> and tracker.<ref name="FC" /> Malar was successful at disrupting Roondha's assassination attempt on Jabba the Hutt with his sniper rifle. The bounty hunter was confident in his ability to outsmart the droid Eightyem.<ref name="Jabba's Palace 1" /> He was also able to pilot starships.<ref name="Jedi Knights 4">[[Jedi Knights 4|''Jedi Knights'' 4]]</ref>

